      "generated_answer": "For an electron spin in a magnetic field, the resonance frequency \\(\\nu\\) is given by  \n\\[\n\\nu = \\frac{g_e \\mu_B B}{h}\n\\]\nWith \\(g_e \\approx 2\\), \\(\\mu_B \\approx 9.274 \\times 10^{-24} \\, \\text{J/T}\\), \\(h \\approx 6.626 \\times 10^{-34} \\, \\text{J·s}\\), and \\(B = 1.0 \\times 10^3 \\, \\text{T}\\) (since \\(1.0 \\,\\mathrm{kT} = 1000 \\,\\mathrm{T}\\)):\n\n\\[\n\\nu \\approx \\frac{(2)(9.274 \\times 10^{-24})(1000)}{6.626 \\times 10^{-34}} \\approx 2.8 \\times 10^{13} \\, \\text{Hz}\n\\]\n\nThat matches option F.  \n\n\\boxed{F}",
