      "generated_answer": "The given limit is:  \n$$\n\\lim_{x \\to 1^-} \\prod_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\left(\\frac{1 + x^{n+1}}{1 + x^n}\\right)^{x^n}\n$$\n\nThis infinite product telescopes: most terms cancel out, leaving a form that simplifies to $ \\exp(1) = e $ as $ x \\to 1^- $, since the logarithm of the product behaves like a Riemann sum converging to 1.\n\nThus, the limit is $ e \\approx 2.7182818 $.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
