    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7664",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the sum of $\\sum_{{n=1}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{{2}}{{n^2 + 4n + 3}}$\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.6333\nB. 0.9333\nC. 2.0333\nD. 0.7333\nE. 0.8333\nF. 1.4333\nG. 2.1433\nH. 0.4333\nI. 0.5633\nJ. 1.2333\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, note that  \n\\[\n\\frac{2}{n^2 + 4n + 3} = \\frac{2}{(n+1)(n+3)}.\n\\]\nPartial fractions give  \n\\[\n\\frac{2}{(n+1)(n+3)} = \\frac{1}{n+1} - \\frac{1}{n+3}.\n\\]  \nThis is a telescoping series:  \n\\[\n\\sum_{n=1}^N \\left( \\frac{1}{n+1} - \\frac{1}{n+3} \\right) \n= \\left( \\frac12 + \\frac13 \\right) - \\left( \\frac{1}{N+2} + \\frac{1}{N+3} \\right).\n\\]  \nTaking \\(N \\to \\infty\\) yields \\(\\frac12 + \\frac13 = \\frac{5}{6} \\approx 0.8333\\).\n\n**Correct choice:** \\(\\boxed{E}\\)",
