  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_math_7484",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For every positive real number $x$, let $g(x)=\\lim _{{r \\rightarrow 0}}((x+1)^{{r+1}}-x^{{r+1}})^{{1/r}}$. What is the limit of $g(x)/x$ as $x$ goes to infinity?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2\nB. Infinity\nC. 3.1415926\nD. 1\nE. 0\nF. 1.6180339\nG. 1.4142135\nH. 1.7320508\nI. 2.7182818\nJ. 3.1415927\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let’s first rewrite \\( g(x) \\) carefully:\n\n\\[\ng(x) = \\lim_{r \\to 0} \\left( (x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1} \\right)^{1/r}.\n\\]\n\nLet \\( A = (x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1} \\).  \nFor small \\( r \\),  \n\\[\n(x+1)^{r+1} = (x+1) e^{(r+1)\\ln(x+1) - (r+1)\\ln x?} \n\\]\nBetter:  \n\\[\n(x+1)^{r+1} = (x+1) e^{(r+1)\\ln(x+1)}?  \n\\]\nActually, \\( (x+1)^{r+1} = e^{(r+1)\\ln(x+1)} \\),  \nand \\( x^{r+1} = e^{(r+1)\\ln x} \\).\n\nBut easier: factor \\( x^{r+1} \\):\n\n\\[\nA = x^{r+1} \\left[ \\left(1+\\frac{1}{x}\\right)^{r+1} - 1 \\right].\n\\]\n\nFor small \\( r \\),  \n\\[\n\\left(1+\\frac{1}{x}\\right)^{r+1} \\approx 1 + (r+1)\\frac{1}{x} + O\\left(\\frac{1}{x^2}\\right).\n\\]\nThus  \n\\[\nA \\approx x^{r+1} \\left[ \\frac{r+1}{x} + O\\left(\\frac{1}{x^2}\\right) \\right].\n\\]\n\nFor small \\( r \\), \\( x^{r+1} = x \\cdot x^r \\), so  \n\n\\[\nA \\approx x \\cdot x^r \\cdot \\frac{r+1}{x} = (r+1) x^r + O(x^{r-1}).\n\\]\n\nSo \\( A \\approx (r+1) x^r \\) as \\( r \\to 0 \\) for large \\( x \\).\n\nThen  \n\\[\ng(x) \\approx \\left[ (r+1) x^r \\right]^{1/r} = (r+1)^{1/r} \\cdot x.\n\\]\n\nBut \\( (r+1)^{1/r} \\to e \\) as \\( r \\to 0 \\).\n\nThus \\( g(x) \\sim e \\cdot x \\), so \\( g(x)/x \\to e \\) as \\( x \\to \\infty \\).\n\nThat matches option **I** \\( = 2.7182818 \\).\n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{I}\\)",
