      "generated_answer": "Merging independent Poisson processes gives \\(N(t)\\) with rate \\(\\lambda = \\lambda_1 + \\lambda_2 = 3\\), and given \\(N(1) = 2\\), the conditional distribution of \\(N_1(1)\\) is binomial:  \n\n\\[\nP(N_1(1) = 1 \\mid N(1) = 2) = \\binom{2}{1}\\left( \\frac{\\lambda_1}{\\lambda_1 + \\lambda_2} \\right)^1 \\left( \\frac{\\lambda_2}{\\lambda_1 + \\lambda_2} \\right)^1\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2 \\times \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{4}{9} \\approx 0.4444\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{D}\n\\]",
