      "generated_answer": "We are working in $\\mathbb{Z}_3$, so coefficients are modulo 3. The quotient ring $\\mathbb{Z}_3[x]/(f(x))$ is a field if and only if $f(x)$ is irreducible over $\\mathbb{Z}_3$. Let $f(x) = x^3 + cx^2 + 1$. We test each $c \\in \\{0, 1, 2\\}$ (since we are in $\\mathbb{Z}_3$) to see when $f(x)$ has no roots (necessary for irreducibility of degree 3). Only $c = 2$ makes $f(x)$ irreducible, as other values give roots. Hence, the correct value is $c = 2$.\n\n$\\boxed{I}$",
