      "generated_answer": "Let \\( g(x) = ax^6 - bx^4 \\).  \nSince \\( x^6 \\) and \\( x^4 \\) are even powers, \\( g(x) \\) is even, so \\( g(2) = g(-2) \\).  \n\nThe linear part is \\( x - 1 \\), so:  \n\\[\nf(2) = g(2) + (2 - 1) = g(2) + 1 = 5 \\implies g(2) = 4.\n\\]  \nThen  \n\\[\nf(-2) = g(-2) + (-2 - 1) = g(2) - 3 = 4 - 3 = 1.\n\\]  \n\nThe correct choice is **B**.  \n\n\\boxed{B}",
