      "generated_answer": "We are given that \\(\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} a_n \\sum_{i=1}^n a_i^2 = 1\\).  \nLet \\(S_n = \\sum_{i=1}^n a_i^2\\). Then \\(a_n S_n \\to 1\\).  \n\nIf \\(a_n\\) is such that \\(S_n\\) grows like \\(n^{\\alpha}\\), then \\(a_n \\sim n^{-\\alpha}\\) and \\(a_n S_n \\sim n^{-\\alpha} n^{\\alpha} = 1\\), consistent. Trying \\(S_n \\sim n^{1/3}\\), then \\(a_n \\sim n^{-1/3}\\).  \nThen \\(3n(a_n)^3 \\sim 3n \\cdot n^{-1} = 3\\).  \n\nHence the limit is **3**.\n\nThe correct letter choice is **A**.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
