-e^{-1.5})^2 = (1-0.22313)^2 = 0.77687^2 = 0.60304\\)  \n\\(e^{-0.5} - e^{-1.5} = 0.606531 - 0.223130 = 0.383401\\)  \nSquare: 0.146934  \nSubtract: \\(0.60304 - 0.146934 = 0.456106\\) ≈ 0.4561 — closest to option F (0.4678), possibly due to rounding difference if using different \\(y_1, y_2\\).  \n\nGiven typical textbook values, \\(y_1=800, y_2=1200\\) maybe yields one of these numbers. But among options, 0.4678 is plausible.\n\nGiven the match from trial values, I’ll pick:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{F}\n\\]",
