      "generated_answer": "The situation describes a population with distinct subgroups (offices in five different countries) where the response variable (views on smoking) is known to vary significantly between groups. Stratified sampling is the appropriate technique because it ensures that each country is represented as a stratum in the sample, accounting for the differences in local social structures and providing a more accurate overall estimate. Unlike cluster sampling, which might randomly exclude specific countries and their distinct perspectives, stratification forces inclusion from every variation group.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
