      "generated_answer": "The only way the product of 5 six-sided dice is not composite is if it is 1 or a prime number. The only possible non-composite product is 1 (when all dice show 1) or a single prime (e.g., one die shows a prime and the rest are 1s), but most such products end up being composite. After analyzing the total number of favorable outcomes (non-composite products), there are only 13 cases (all 1s, or exactly one die showing 2, 3, or 5 and the rest 1s), so total non-composite outcomes = 1 (all 1s) + 3×5 = 16. Thus, non-composite probability = 16⁄7776, so composite probability = 1 − 16⁄7776 = 7760⁄7776 = 485⁄486.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
