    "global index": "MathQA_2450",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: ( 3 x + 2 ) ( 2 x - 1 ) = ax ^ 2 + kx + n . what is the value of a - n + k ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5\nB. 8\nC. 9\nD. 10\nE. 11\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, expand \\((3x + 2)(2x - 1)\\):  \n\\(3x \\cdot 2x = 6x^2\\)  \n\\(3x \\cdot (-1) = -3x\\)  \n\\(2 \\cdot 2x = 4x\\)  \n\\(2 \\cdot (-1) = -2\\)  \n\nSo \\(6x^2 + (-3x + 4x) - 2 = 6x^2 + x - 2\\).  \nThus \\(a = 6\\), \\(k = 1\\), \\(n = -2\\).  \n\nCompute \\(a - n + k = 6 - (-2) + 1 = 6 + 2 + 1 = 9\\).  \n\n\\boxed{C}",
