      "generated_answer": "The total surface area of a solid hemisphere is given by the formula $ 3\\pi r^2 $, where $ r $ is the radius. Given the diameter is 14 cm, the radius $ r = 7 $ cm. Substituting, we get $ 3 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 7^2 = 3 \\times 22 \\times 7 = 462 \\text{ cm}^2 $.\n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{A}",
