    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: n = 1 ! + 2 ! + 3 ! . . . . . + 10 ! . what is the last digit of n ^ n ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3\nB. 4\nC. 5\nD. 6\nE. 7\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, factorials from \\(5!\\) onward end with digit 0 because they contain both \\(2\\) and \\(5\\) as factors.  \nSo \\(n = 1! + 2! + 3! + 4! +\\) (terms ending in 0 from \\(5!\\) to \\(10!\\)).  \n\\(1!+2!+3!+4! = 1+2+6+24=33\\), so \\(n\\) ends in \\(3\\).\n\nNow \\(n^n\\) ends in the same digit as \\(3^n\\) mod 10. For \\(n \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4}\\)?  \n\\(n\\) ends in 3 ⇒ \\(n \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4}\\).  \nCyclicity of last digit of powers of 3: \\(3^1 \\to 3, 3^2\\to 9, 3^3\\to7, 3^4\\to1\\), repeat.  \nIf \\(n \\bmod 4 = 3\\), then \\(3^n\\) ends in \\(7\\).\n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{E}\\)",
