    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the price of shoes be \\( s \\) and the price of boots be \\( b \\).  \nFrom the given data:  \n\\( 22s + 16b = 540 \\) … (1)  \n\\( 8s + 32b = 720 \\) … (2)  \n\nMultiply (1) by 2: \\( 44s + 32b = 1080 \\).  \nSubtract (2) from this: \\( (44s - 8s) = 1080 - 720 \\) → \\( 36s = 360 \\) → \\( s = 10 \\).  \nFrom (2): \\( 80 + 32b = 720 \\) → \\( 32b = 640 \\) → \\( b = 20 \\).  \n\nBoots cost \\( 20 - 10 = 10 \\) dollars more than shoes.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{C}",
