    "global index": "MathQA_518",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: if f ( f ( n ) ) + f ( n ) = 2 n + 3 and f ( 0 ) = 1 , what is the value of f ( 2012 ) ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 222\nB. 2787\nC. 2013\nD. 2778\nE. 10222\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let’s break this down.  \n\nWe are told \\( f(f(n)) + f(n) = 2n + 3 \\) and \\( f(0) = 1 \\).  \n\nFirst, plug \\( n = 0 \\) into the functional equation:  \n\\[\nf(f(0)) + f(0) = 2(0) + 3 \\implies f(1) + 1 = 3 \\implies f(1) = 2.\n\\]  \n\nNow plug \\( n = 1 \\):  \n\\[\nf(f(1)) + f(1) = 2(1) + 3 \\implies f(2) + 2 = 5 \\implies f(2) = 3.\n\\]  \n\nPlug \\( n = 2 \\):  \n\\[\nf(f(2)) + f(2) = 2(2) + 3 \\implies f(3) + 3 = 7 \\implies f(3) = 4.\n\\]  \n\nWe see a pattern \\( f(n) = n+1 \\) for \\( n = 0, 1, 2, 3 \\).  \n\nAssume \\( f(n) = n+1 \\) for all \\( n \\) — check if it satisfies the functional equation:  \n\\( f(f(n)) = f(n+1) = (n+1)+1 = n+2 \\),  \nthen \\( f(f(n)) + f(n) = (n+2) + (n+1) = 2n+3 \\), yes — it works.  \n\nThus \\( f(2012) = 2012 + 1 = 2013 \\).  \n\nAnswer matches option **C**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{C}\n\\]",
