      "generated_answer": "We are told that from point $ r $, walking 50 km further reaches point $ s $, and $ s $ is equidistant from $ r $ and $ q $. So, $ rs = sq = 50 $ km, meaning $ rq = rs + sq = 100 $ km. Also, $ pr = \\frac{1}{2} rq = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 100 = 50 $ km. Therefore, total distance $ pq = pr + rq = 50 + 100 = 150 $ km.\n\n$\\boxed{A}$",
