    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The minimum bit interval of 1 μs corresponds to a bit rate of 1/1×10⁻⁶ = 1 Mbps (10⁶ bps). Each voice channel has a bandwidth of 3 kHz, so by Nyquist, the sampling rate is 6 kHz. With 16 quantization levels (4 bits per sample), each voice channel requires 6,000 × 4 = 24 kbps. Dividing total capacity (1 Mbps) by 24 kbps gives 1,000,000 / 24,000 ≈ 41.67, so approximately 45 channels can be multiplexed.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
