    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10193",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A card is drawn at random from a deck of cards. Find the probability that at least one of the following three events will occur: Event A : a heart is drawn. Event B: a card which is not a face card is drawn. Event C: the number of spots (if any) on the drawn card is divisible by 3.\n\nOptions: \nA. 40/52\nB. 31/52\nC. 33/52\nD. 44/52\nE. 45/52\nF. 43/52\nG. 30/52\nH. 38/52\nI. 41/52\nJ. 35/52\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are asked to find the probability that **at least one** of the three events occurs when a card is drawn from a standard 52-card deck:\n\n- **Event A**: a heart is drawn → 13 hearts in the deck.  \n- **Event B**: a card which is **not a face card** → there are 12 face cards (3 per suit: J, Q, K), so 52 − 12 = 40 non-face cards.  \n- **Event C**: the number of spots is divisible by 3. This applies to numbered cards (2 through 10), and numbers divisible by 3 are 3, 6, 9. So 3, 6, 9 in each suit → 3 values × 4 suits = 12 cards.\n\nWe are to find $ P(A \\cup B \\cup C) $. Since it's easier to compute the complement (none of the events occur) and subtract from 1, let's find the number of cards that satisfy **none** of the three events:\n\n- **Not A**: not a heart → must be in clubs, diamonds, or spades → 39 cards.  \n- **Not B**: is a face card → 12 face cards in total.  \n- **Not C**: spot number **not** divisible by 3. But note: face cards don't have \"numbers\", so \"spot number divisible by 3\" applies only to numbered cards (2–10). So for **Not C**, we include cards that are face cards or numbered cards not divisible by 3.\n\nBut for **none** of the events to occur, all three must fail:\n\n- Fail A: card is **not a heart** → clubs, diamonds, spades (39 cards)  \n- Fail B: card **is a face card** (12 total: J, Q, K of each suit)  \n- Fail C: card is either a face card or has a number **not** divisible by 3. But since we’re already requiring it to be a face card (to fail B), then **all face cards automatically fail C** (because C only applies to numbered cards, so face cards don't satisfy C). So failing C is automatic if it's a face card.\n\nBut note: For **Not C**, we are interpreting that the number being divisible by 3 is **false**. Since face cards have no number (or no \"spots\"), they **do not** satisfy \"number divisible by 3\", so they **do not** belong to event C. So **face cards are not in C**, meaning they **fail C**.\n\nSo the cards that fail **A**, **B**, and **C** are:\n- Not a heart (so clubs, diamonds, spades) **and**\n- Is a face card (so must be J, Q, K of clubs, diamonds, or spades)\n\nThere are 3 suits (non-hearts), and 3 face cards per suit → $3 \\times 3 = 9$ cards.\n\nSo only **9 cards** fail all three events.\n\nTherefore, number of cards that satisfy **at least one** of A, B, or C is:  \n$52 - 9 = 43$\n\nSo probability = $ \\frac{43}{52} $\n\n\\boxed{F}",
