    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If six messages having probabilities (1 / 4), (1 / 4), (1 / 8), (1 / 8), (1 / 8) and (1 / 8) can be accommodated in a single communication system, determine the entropy.\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.00 bits/message\nB. 2.25 bits/message\nC. 1.75 bits/message\nD. 3.00 bits/message\nE. 2.75 bits/message\nF. 3.25 bits/message\nG. 4.00 bits/message\nH. 3.50 bits/message\nI. 2.50 bits/message\nJ. 1.50 bits/message\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The entropy is calculated using \\( H = -\\sum p_i \\log_2 p_i \\).  \n\nGiven probabilities:  \n\\[\n\\frac14, \\frac14, \\frac18, \\frac18, \\frac18, \\frac18\n\\]  \n\\[\nH = - \\left[ 2\\left(\\frac14 \\log_2 \\frac14\\right) + 4\\left(\\frac18 \\log_2 \\frac18\\right) \\right]\n= - \\left[ 2\\left(\\frac14 \\times (-2)\\right) + 4\\left(\\frac18 \\times (-3)\\right) \\right]\n= 1 + 1.5 = 2.5 \\text{ bits/message}\n\\]  \n\nThis matches option I.  \n\n\\boxed{I}",
