    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We start with  \n\n\\[\nF(s) = \\frac{8s + 2}{s^2 + 3s + 2}\n\\]  \nFactor the denominator:  \n\\[\ns^2 + 3s + 2 = (s+1)(s+2)\n\\]  \nWrite the partial fractions as  \n\\[\n\\frac{8s+2}{(s+1)(s+2)} = \\frac{A}{s+1} + \\frac{B}{s+2}\n\\]  \nMultiply through by \\((s+1)(s+2)\\):  \n\\[\n8s+2 = A(s+2) + B(s+1)\n\\]  \n\\[\n8s+2 = (A+B)s + (2A + B)\n\\]  \nEquating coefficients:  \n\\[\nA + B = 8,\\quad 2A + B = 2\n\\]  \nSubtract the first from the second: \\(A = -6\\), then \\(B = 14\\).  \n\nThus  \n\\[\nF(s) = \\frac{-6}{s+1} + \\frac{14}{s+2}\n\\]  \nThis matches option **H**.  \n\n\\boxed{H}",
