    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10789",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Evaluate f(t) if F(s) = [(2s^2 + 13s + 17) / {{(s + 1)(s + 3)}}]\n\nOptions: \nA. 2\\delta(t) + (3e^-t + e^-3t)u(t)\nB. 2\\delta(t) + (3e^-t + 2e^-3t)u(t)\nC. 3\\delta(t) + (3e^-t + 2e^-3t)u(t)\nD. 2 + (3e^-t + 2e^-3t)u(t)\nE. 2 + (5e^-t + 2e^-3t)\nF. 2\\delta(t) + (3e^-t + 2e^-3t)\nG. (3e^-t + 2e^-3t)u(t)\nH. 2\\delta(t) + (3e^-2t + 2e^-3t)u(t)\nI. 2\\delta(t) + (4e^-t + 3e^-3t)u(t)\nJ. 2\\delta(t) + (5e^-t + 2e^-3t)u(t)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, \\( F(s) \\) is not strictly proper since numerator and denominator degrees are equal (degree 2).  \nThus, perform long division:  \n\\[\n\\frac{2s^2 + 13s + 17}{(s+1)(s+3)} = \\frac{2s^2 + 13s + 17}{s^2 + 4s + 3}.\n\\]  \nDividing gives \\( 2 \\) plus remainder:  \n\\[\n2 + \\frac{5s + 11}{(s+1)(s+3)}.\n\\]  \nPartial fractions on \\(\\frac{5s+11}{(s+1)(s+3)}\\) yield \\(\\frac{3}{s+1} + \\frac{2}{s+3}\\).  \n\nSo \\( F(s) = 2 + \\frac{3}{s+1} + \\frac{2}{s+3} \\), which corresponds to \\( f(t) = 2\\delta(t) + \\left(3e^{-t} + 2e^{-3t}\\right) u(t) \\).  \n\nThe correct choice matches option **B**.  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{B}\n\\]",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 320,
        "output_tokens": 244,
