    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Since \\( f(t) = \\sin(2\\pi t) \\) has a frequency of 1 Hz, the Nyquist sampling rate must be greater than 2 samples/sec. Among the options, the sampling rate should allow proper digitization into 4 bits, requiring that the counting rate be high enough to cover the voltage range during one sample period. Option F (4 samples/sec, 200 V/sec ramp slope, 2000 counts/sec) gives a clear match: 4 Hz is above Nyquist for 1 Hz, and the counting rate divided by sampling rate gives \\(2000/4 = 500\\) counts per sample, which comfortably exceeds the \\(2^4 = 16\\) which fits \\(2^4 = 16\\) quantization levels.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
