    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10176",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the Laplace transform L{{g(t)}}, where g(t)= 0,t < 4 and= (t - 4)^2,t \\geq 4\n\nOptions: \nA. [(2e^-4s) / s^3]\nB. 2 / s^3\nC. (2 / s^2) * e^-4s\nD. 4 / s^3\nE. [(2e^-4s) / s^4]\nF. (2 / s^3) * e^-s\nG. e^-4s\nH. [(e^-4s) / s^2]\nI. (2 / s) * e^-4s\nJ. (t^2 - 8t + 16) / s\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The function \\( g(t) = (t-4)^2 \\) for \\( t \\geq 4 \\) with \\( g(t)=0 \\) for \\( t<4 \\) is a shifted quadratic.  \nIts Laplace transform is obtained using the time‑shift property: \\( L\\{ (t-4)^2 u(t-4) \\} = e^{-4s} L\\{ t^2 \\} = e^{-4s} \\frac{2}{s^3}. \\)  \nThis matches option **A**.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
