    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "For question (1), with a 1.5-kW load from a 230-V AC source at unity power factor, the AC input current is $ I = \\frac{1500}{230} \\approx 6.52 $ A, closest to 6.5 A. The DC output voltage for a full-wave rectifier is approximately $ V_{dc} = 0.9 \\times V_{ac} \\times \\sqrt{2} \\approx 310 $ V, and $ I_{dc} = \\frac{1500}{310} \\approx 4.84 $ A. For question (2), in inverting mode with 230 V DC input, the AC output voltage is roughly $ V_{ac} = \\frac{V_{dc}}{1.11} \\approx 200 $ V, giving AC current $ \\frac{2500}{200} = 12.5 $ A and DC current $ \\frac{2500}{230} \\approx 10.87 $ A, matching option D most closely.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
