      "generated_answer": "The given probability density function is that of a Rayleigh distribution with parameter $\\alpha$. For a Rayleigh-distributed random variable $R$, the expected value is $E[R] = \\alpha \\sqrt{\\pi/2}$, the second moment is $E[R^2] = 2\\alpha^2$, and the variance is $\\sigma^2 = E[R^2] - (E[R])^2 = 2\\alpha^2 - (\\alpha^2 \\pi/2) = \\alpha^2(2 - \\pi/2) \\approx \\alpha^2(0.43)$. These values match option F exactly.\n\n$\\boxed{F}$",
