    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10939",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given the Laplace transform of i(t), L[i(t)] = I(s) = [{{E - V(0^+)}} / {{R(s + (1 / RC))}}] Determine i(0^+).\n\nOptions: \nA. [{{E / (v(0^+) * R)}}]\nB. [{{v(0^+) - E}} / R]\nC. [{{E * v(0^+)}} / R]\nD. [{{E - v(0^+)}} * R]\nE. [{{E * R}} / {{v(0^+) - 1}}]\nF. [{{E + R}} / {{v(0^+) + RC}}]\nG. [{{(E - v(0^+)) / (R + RC)}}]\nH. [{{E + v(0^+)}} / R]\nI. [{{E * (v(0^+) + 1)}} / R]\nJ. [{{E - v(0^+)}} / R]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We use the initial value theorem for Laplace transforms:  \n$i(0^+) = \\lim_{s \\to \\infty} sI(s)$.  \nGiven $ I(s) = \\frac{E - V(0^+)}{R(s + 1/(RC))} $, multiplying by $ s $ and taking the limit as $ s \\to \\infty $:  \n$ sI(s) = \\frac{s(E - V(0^+))}{R(s + 1/(RC))} \\to \\frac{E - V(0^+)}{R} $ as $ s \\to \\infty $.  \n\nThus, $ i(0^+) = \\frac{E - V(0^+)}{R} $, which matches option J.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
      "success": true,
