      "generated_answer": "The divergence in spherical coordinates for a field \\( \\mathbf{A} = kr^n \\hat{\\mathbf{r}} \\) is  \n\\[\n\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{A} = \\frac{1}{r^2} \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial r}\\left(r^2 A_r\\right) = \\frac{1}{r^2} \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial r} (k r^{n+2}) = k(n+2) r^{n-1}.\n\\]  \nIntegrating over a sphere of radius \\(a\\) gives  \n\\[\n\\int_V \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{A} \\, dV = k(n+2) \\int_0^a r^{n-1} (4\\pi r^2) dr = 4\\pi k (n+2) \\int_0^a r^{n+1} dr.\n\\]  \nThis yields \\(4\\pi k a^{n+2}\\) when \\(n+1 > -1\\) (assuming \\(n\\) is such that the integral converges).\n\nThe correct answer is therefore **A**.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{A}\n\\]",
