    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A carrier with amplitude 4 volts and frequencyf_c= 2MHz is frequency modulated by a modulating signal m(t) = sin 1000\\pit. The amplitude of the modulating signal is 2 volts and the frequency deviation was found to be equal to 1 kHz. If the amplitude and frequency of the modulating signal are increased to 8 volts and 2 kHz respectively, write an expression for the new modulated signal.\n\nOptions: \nA. v(t) = 4cos(4\\pi × 10^6 t + 2 sin2\\pi × 2000t)\nB. v(t) = 8cos(4π × 10^6 t + 4 sin2π × 1000t)\nC. v(t) = 8cos(2π × 10^6 t + 4 sin2π × 2000t)\nD. v(t) = 8cos(4π × 10^6 t + 8 sin2π × 2000t)\nE. v(t) = 4cos(4π × 10^6 t + 16 sin2π × 2000t)\nF. v(t) = 4cos(4π × 10^6 t + 4 sin2π × 1000t)\nG. v(t) = 4cos(2\\pi × 10^6 t + 2 sin2\\pi × 2000t)\nH. v(t) = 4cos(4\\pi × 10^6 t + 4 sin2\\pi × 2000t)\nI. v(t) = 8cos(4\\pi × 10^6 t + 2 sin2\\pi × 2000t)\nJ. v(t) = 4cos(4π × 10^6 t + 8 sin2π × 2000t)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
