    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10461",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The nonlinear characteristic of a capacitor is given by q(t) = 0.5\\nu^2 (t) The voltage across this capacitor is given by \\nu(t) = 1 + 0.5 sin t Find the current through this capacitor.\n\nOptions: \nA. i(t) = 0.5cos t + 0.25 sin 2t\nB. i(t) = .5cos 2t + .125 sin 2t\nC. i(t) = 0.5cos 2t + 0.125 cos t\nD. i(t) = .5sin + .125 cos 2t\nE. i(t) = 1.0cos t + 0.125 sin 2t\nF. i(t) = .5cost + .125 sin t\nG. i(t) = .5cost + .125 sin 2t\nH. i(t) = ν(t)sin t + 0.125 cos t\nI. i(t) = ν(t)cos t + 0.25 sin t\nJ. i(t) = 0.5sin t + 0.125 sin t\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We have \\( q(t) = 0.5\\, \\nu(t)^2 \\) and \\( \\nu(t) = 1 + 0.5\\sin t \\).  \nCurrent is \\( i(t) = \\frac{dq}{dt} = \\nu(t) \\frac{d\\nu}{dt} \\) because \\( \\frac{dq}{d\\nu} = \\nu \\).  \n\nFirst, \\( \\frac{d\\nu}{dt} = 0.5\\cos t \\).  \nSo \\( i(t) = (1 + 0.5\\sin t)(0.5\\cos t) = 0.5\\cos t + 0.25\\sin t \\cos t \\).  \nUsing \\( \\sin t\\cos t = 0.5\\sin 2t \\), we get \\( i(t) = 0.5\\cos t + 0.125\\sin 2t \\).  \n\nThat matches option **G** exactly.  \n\n\\boxed{G}",
