    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let it be required to find the square roots of A where A = 3.08 + j8.455.\n\nOptions: \nA. 4∠35° and 4∠215°\nB. 2∠40° and 2∠220°\nC. 3.5∠45° and 3.5∠225°\nD. 2.8∠33° and 2.8∠213°\nE. 3∠45° and 3∠225°\nF. 3∠40° and 3∠220°\nG. 2.5∠30° and 2.5∠210°\nH. 3∠35° and 3∠215°\nI. 3∠30° and 3∠210°\nJ. 3∠50° and 3∠230°\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given a complex number $ A = 3.08 + j8.455 $. First, convert it to polar form:  \nMagnitude: $ |A| = \\sqrt{3.08^2 + 8.455^2} \\approx \\sqrt{9.486 + 71.487} \\approx \\sqrt{80.973} \\approx 8.998 \\approx 9 $,  \nAngle: $ \\theta = \\tan^{-1}(8.455 / 3.08) \\approx \\tan^{-1}(2.745) \\approx 70^\\circ $. So $ A \\approx 3 \\angle 70^\\circ $ in polar form (but wait — magnitude is ~9, so $ A \\approx 9 \\angle 70^\\circ $).\n\nThe square roots will have magnitude $ \\sqrt{9} = 3 $ and angles $ 70^\\circ/2 = 35^\\circ $ and $ 35^\\circ + 180^\\circ = 215^\\circ $. Thus, the roots are $ 3\\angle35^\\circ $ and $ 3\\angle215^\\circ $.\n\nThis matches option **H**.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
