    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A flat key is used to prevent slipping of a cast-iron gear mounted on a shaft, 2 in. in diameter. Determine the appropriate dimensions of the key if the gear delivers 125 hp at 250 rpm. Assume design stresses for shear and bearing as 19,000 psi and 37,000 psi.\n\nOptions: \nA. key thickness = 3/8 in., key width = 1/2 in., key length = 3.32 in.\nB. key thickness = 1/4 in., key width = 3/8 in., key length = 6.0 in.\nC. key thickness = 3/8 in., key width = 1/2 in., key length = 4.6 in.\nD. key thickness = 1/2 in., key width = 1/4 in., key length = 4.0 in.\nE. key thickness = 3/8 in., key width = 5/8 in., key length = 5.0 in.\nF. key thickness = 5/8 in., key width = 3/8 in., key length = 3.32 in.\nG. key thickness = 1/4 in., key width = 5/8 in., key length = 3.5 in.\nH. key thickness = 1/2 in., key width = 1/2 in., key length = 4.6 in.\nI. key thickness = 3/8 in., key width = 3/8 in., key length = 2.5 in.\nJ. key thickness = 1/2 in., key width = 3/8 in., key length = 4.6 in.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, calculate the torque transmitted:  \n$ T = \\frac{63025 \\times \\text{hp}}{\\text{rpm}} = \\frac{63025 \\times 125}{250} = 31,512.5 $ in-lb.  \n\nShear stress governs key width and length: $ \\tau = \\frac{T}{r \\times w \\times l} $, where $ r = 1 $ in, $ \\tau = 19,000 $ psi. Solving for $ w \\times l $:  \n$ w \\times l = \\frac{31,512.5}{1 \\times 19,000} \\approx 1.658 $.  \n\nAssuming standard key proportions (for 2\" shaft, std. key width = 1/2 in, thickness = 3/8 in), check length: $ l = 1.658 / 0.5 = 3.32 $ in for shear. Bearing stress check: $ \\sigma_b = \\frac{T}{r \\times (t/2) \\times l} = \\frac{31,512.5}{1 \\times (0.375/2) \\times l} $, needs to be ≤ 37,000 psi → $ l \\geq \\frac{31,512.5}{1 \\times 0.1875 \\times 37,000} \\approx 4.54 $ in. So length must be ≥ ~4.54 in. Option A has length 3.32 — too short. Option C has same key but length 4.6 in — sufficient for bearing. Thus, **C** is correct.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
