    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, determine the Laplace transform of the input $v(t) = 16e^{-3t}u(t)$, which is $V(s) = \\frac{16}{s+3}$. Substituting this into the expression for $V_{ab}(s) = \\frac{3V(s) + 3s + 27}{s^2 + 6s + 8}$ and simplifying the numerator results in $V_{ab}(s) = \\frac{3s^2 + 36s + 129}{(s+3)(s+2)(s+4)}$. Using partial fraction expansion, the coefficients for the poles at $s=-3, -2, -4$ are calculated to be $A=-48, B=\\frac{69}{2},$ and $C=\\frac{33}{2}$ respectively. The inverse Laplace transform of these terms corresponds exactly to Option J.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
