      "generated_answer": "For a mine hoist lifting up to 5 tons, a robust wire rope with appropriate fatigue resistance is required. A 6 × 19 plow steel wire rope typically requires a sheave diameter of at least 18–22 times the rope diameter for acceptable fatigue life, and larger diameters improve bend life. Option C provides a reasonable rope diameter (7/8 in), a compatible sheave (21 in, ~24× rope diameter), and a realistic bend life of 50,000, making it the best choice.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
