      "generated_answer": "The speed ratio is $ \\frac{1400}{700} = 2 $, so the driven sprocket must have twice as many teeth as the driving sprocket. Among the options, all pairs maintain a 1:2 ratio, so we consider best practice: a driving sprocket with fewer than 17 teeth may wear excessively, and for smooth operation and rust-proofing, proper lubrication (type B or D) is needed. However, lubrication type B (bath lubrication) is typically recommended for moderate speeds and triple strand chains, and option A has 11 and 22 teeth with lubrication type B, which is reasonable for this application.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
