    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An equation of state due toDietericiis P(V -nb')exp [na' / (RTV)] =nRT(1) Evaluate the constants a' and b' in terms of the critical constants P_c,V_c, andT_cof a gas.\n\nOptions: \nA. a' = 2RT_cV_c, b' = (2*V_c)\nB. a' = P_cV_c^2, b' = V_c / 3\nC. a' = RT_c^2 / P_c, b' = V_c / P_c\nD. a' = 2RT_cV_c, b' = (V_c/ 2)\nE. a' = 2RT_c, b' = V_c\nF. a' = RT_c / P_c, b' = 2V_c\nG. a' = P_cV_c / T_c, b' = 3V_c\nH. a' = RT_cV_c, b' = V_c\nI. a' = 4RT_c / V_c, b' = V_c / 4\nJ. a' = 2P_cV_c^2 / T_c, b' = V_c / 8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
