    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, the reaction given is actually for ethene (C₂H₄), not ethane (C₂H₆), but we’ll proceed with C₂H₄ based on the equation.  \n\nBalancing: C₂H₄ + 3 O₂ → 2 CO₂ + 2 H₂O.  \nMolar mass C₂H₄ = (2×12)+(4×1) = 28 g/mol.  \nGiven 84 g → 84/28 = 3 mol C₂H₄.  \nEach mole C₂H₄ produces 2 mol CO₂ → 3×2 = 6 mol CO₂.  \nMolar mass CO₂ = 44 g/mol → 6×44 = 264 g CO₂.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{G}",
