      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}.\n\nReducing the sample size from 1000 to 500 decreases the statistical power of the study to detect a true difference. A decrease in power directly translates to an increased probability of making a Type II error (failing to reject the null hypothesis when it is false), which corresponds to the parameter $\\beta$ mentioned in the text. In contrast, the chance of a Type I error is typically fixed by the significance level ($\\alpha$), and \"false negative\" is terminology more commonly associated with diagnostic testing rather than interventional clinical trial hypotheses.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
