      "generated_answer": "The data show that racial and ethnic minorities had significantly more \"missed opportunities\" for influenza vaccination in office-based settings compared to non-Hispanic whites, and eliminating these missed opportunities could reduce disparities by about half. This suggests that routine offering of vaccines during office visits—where patients are already present and willing to be vaccinated if recommended—would close a substantial portion of the gap. Therefore, routine offering in these settings is likely an effective strategy to reduce disparities.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
