      "generated_answer": "The study found no significant differences between peak oxygen uptake during treadmill testing and oxygen uptake during supramaximal testing, suggesting that $\\dot{V}O_2$peak is a valid indicator of $\\dot{V}O_2$max in ambulatory children with spina bifida. Although five children showed improvement in oxygen uptake during supramaximal testing, most met standard criteria for maximal effort. Therefore, the evidence supports that peak oxygen uptake reflects maximum oxygen uptake in this population.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
