s to the Project Gutenberg Literary\nArchive Foundation, how to help produce our new eBooks, and how to\nsubscribe to our email newsletter to hear about new eBooks.\n\n\nQuestion: How does Hunca Munca pay for what she did? \n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Hunca Munca does not pay money for what she did; instead, she and Tom Thumb feel remorseful after their rampage in the doll's house. To make amends, Hunca Munca cleans the doll's house every day with a duster and a broom, striving to be helpful despite their earlier mischief. \n\n\\boxed{\\text{Hunca Munca makes amends by cleaning the doll's house daily.}}",
