  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4592",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"The challenge of the next half century is whether we have the wisdom to use wealth to enrich and elevate our national life, and to advance the quality of our American civilization….The Great Society rests on abundance and liberty for all. It demands an end to poverty and racial injustice, to which we are totally committed in our time. But that is just the beginning. The Great Society is a place where every child can find knowledge to enrich his mind and to enlarge his talents. It is a place where leisure is a welcome chance to build and reflect, not a feared cause of boredom and restlessness. It is a place where the city of man serves not only the needs of the body and the demands of commerce but the desire for beauty and the hunger for community. It is a place where man can renew contact with nature. It is a place which honors creation for its own sake and for what it adds to the understanding of the race. It is a place where men are more concerned with the quality of their goals than the quantity of their goods. But most of all, the Great Society is not a safe harbor, a resting place, a final objective, a finished work. It is a challenge constantly renewed, beckoning us toward a destiny where the meaning of our lives matches the marvelous products of our labor.\"\nLyndon Johnson, Remarks at the University of Michigan, Ann Arbor, 1964\nAlong with his goals of establishing a Great Society, Johnson was also engaged in which of the following initiatives?\n\nOptions: \nA. Undermining Communism in Korea with the Korean War\nB. Undermining Communism in Russia during the Cuban Missile Crisis\nC. Undermining Communism in China with the Cultural Revolution\nD. Undermining Communism in Afghanistan with the Soviet-Afghan War\nE. Undermining Communism in East Germany with the Berlin Airlift\nF. Undermining Communism in the Eastern Block by demanding a removal of the Berlin Wall\nG. Undermining Communism in Cuba with the Bay of Pigs Invasion\nH. Undermining Communism in Laos with the Laotian Civil War\nI. Undermining Communism in Turkey and Greece using economic aid\nJ. Undermining Communism in Vietnam after the Tet Offensive\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3.5-9b",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Lyndon B. Johnson's presidency (1963–1969) is historically defined by the domestic Great Society and the foreign policy escalation of the Vietnam War, which included his administration's engagement following the 1968 Tet Offensive. The other options describe events associated with the Truman or Kennedy administrations or later time periods in Cold War history. Therefore, the Vietnam War is the only initiative Johnson was engaged in that aligns with this timeline.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
      "success": true,
