      "generated_answer": "Sukarno's speech emphasizes peace, independence, and the collective moral and political strength of Asia and Africa, reflecting the core principles of the Non-Aligned Movement during the Cold War. The Bandung Conference of 1955 was a pivotal moment for newly independent nations seeking to avoid alignment with either the United States or the Soviet Union. Therefore, the correct answer is the geopolitical context in which neutrality was most actively pursued by these leaders.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
