 by a council elected by the King\nJ. A colony in which the King granted a charter to a single businessman\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3.5-9b",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Pennsylvania is historically classified as a proprietary colony because King Charles II granted governing rights and land to William Penn as an individual proprietor rather than to a company or the Crown itself. This system allowed Penn to issue charters and establish government frameworks for the inhabitants, as evidenced by the provided text. Consequently, option F is the most accurate historical description of the colony's structure.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
