      "generated_answer": "The key difference is that complex foragers intensively exploit a limited number of high-yield resources, often leading to more sedentary lifestyles and social complexity, unlike simple foragers who rely on a broad range of wild foods. Option B correctly identifies this characteristic of complex foragers. Other options incorrectly attribute agricultural or technological practices to foragers that typically belong to food-producing societies.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
