      "generated_answer": "Based on the text and context, the Act of Supremacy explicitly made the English monarch the supreme head of the Church of England, directly challenging papal authority. This aligns most clearly with the goal of consolidating royal power over the church and discrediting the Pope's authority in England.  \n\n**Correct choice:** \\boxed{G}",
