      "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}.\n\nThe provided text explicitly calls for the establishment of \"industrial justice\" and prioritizing the \"public welfare.\" The Underwood-Simmons Tariff of 1913 lowered import duties to reduce consumer costs and support fair competition between businesses, which aligned directly with the Progressive goal of ensuring industrial justice. Consequently, Progressives endorsed the tariff as a legislative step to protect the general interest over special corporate interests.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
