      "generated_answer": "The Sumerian text from *The Epic of Gilgamesh* describes the afterlife as a dark, joyless place of dust and clay, while the Egyptian *Maxims of Ptahhotep* emphasizes truth, divine guidance, and a more ordered, hopeful moral universe. This contrast suggests that the Egyptians held a more optimistic and less gloomy view of existence, particularly in relation to the afterlife. Therefore, the best-supported conclusion is:\n\n\\boxed{G}",
