      "generated_answer": "The narrator mentions \"Rhine and Prague\" to emphasize the territories the Winter King must now avoid after his failed claim to the Bohemian throne. These locations were central to the Holy Roman Empire and symbolized imperial authority, contrasting the Winter King’s illegitimate rule. The correct answer is **B**, as it best reflects the political warning in the context of the song.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
