      "generated_answer": "The phrase \"The birds and beasts . . . enjoyed their existence according to their nature\" reflects the Daoist ideal of harmony with the natural order and living in accordance with one's true nature. This concept aligns closely with Daoist beliefs that emphasize spontaneity, simplicity, and alignment with the Dao (the natural way of the universe). While the passage is Confucian in tone overall, this specific phrase resonates with foundational Daoist principles.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
