    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}\nThe text highlights Tacitus's view that the internal conflict among the Germanic tribes is a strategic benefit to the Roman Empire because it prevents them from uniting. This strategic preference demonstrates that Roman authorities feared a united Germanic force would threaten their security. Therefore, the views expressed serve as evidence of the concern about potential barbarian attacks on the empire's frontier.",
