      "generated_answer": "The fossil record from 1.8 million to 400,000 years ago shows significant morphological diversity across regions, with forms such as Homo erectus in Asia, Homo heidelbergensis in Europe, and similar populations in Africa, suggesting regional variation and speciation. Researchers generally interpret this pattern as evidence for multiple related species evolving from earlier African ancestors but diverging geographically. Thus, the best-supported answer is:\n\n\\boxed{H}",
