      "generated_answer": "The passage discusses how economic necessity led women to enter public life, including working and dining unescorted, reflecting broader social changes tied to women's independence and public participation. This shift is most directly connected to the women's suffrage movement and the legal recognition of women's rights, culminating in the right to vote. \n\nThe most directly related option is the 19th Amendment, which granted women the right to vote and symbolized their growing public and economic role.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
      "success": true,
