    "cost": 0.00047474999999999997,
    "accuracy": 1.0,
    "for_optimality": false
  },
  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4645",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"We found that not only was it a civil war, an effort by a people who had for years been seeking their liberation from any colonial influence whatsoever, but also we found that the Vietnamese whom we had enthusiastically molded after our own image were hard put to take up the fight against the threat we were supposedly saving them from.\n\"We found most people didn't even know the difference between communism and democracy. They only wanted to work in rice paddies without helicopters strafing them and bombs with napalm burning their villages and tearing their country apart. They wanted everything to do with the war, particularly with this foreign presence of the United States of America, to leave them alone in peace, and they practiced the art of survival by siding with whichever military force was present at a particular time, be it Viet Cong, North Vietnamese or American.\"\nJohn Kerry, 1971\nThe most important factor in the defeat of Democratic presidential candidates in the elections of 1952 and 1968 was\n\nOptions: \nA. the candidates' lack of military service records\nB. the rise of third-party candidates that split the Democratic vote\nC. the American public's desire to avoid conflict and return to a more conservative political and social life\nD. the Democratic Party's perceived weakness on national security issues\nE. the Democratic candidates' controversial positions on civil rights legislation\nF. the Democratic candidates' inability to effectively communicate their policies to the public\nG. the Democratic Party's unequivocal support of the Equal Rights Amendment\nH. the Democratic Party platform pledge to increase taxes in order to pay off the national debt\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3.5-9b",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{C}\nThe excerpt from John Kerry highlights the public's disillusionment with the Vietnam War and a strong desire for peace (\"to leave them alone in peace\"). This sentiment of war fatigue mirrored the public mood in both the 1952 (post-Korean War) and 1968 (Vietnam War) elections, where voters favored candidates who promised to end conflict and restore stability. Therefore, the American public's desire to avoid conflict and return to a more conservative political and social life was the primary factor in the Democrats' losses.",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 404,
        "output_tokens": 4240,
        "total_tokens": 4644
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": 0.0006562,
    "accuracy": 1.0,
    "for_optimality": false
  },
  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4646",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: This question refers to the following information.\n\"Permit us, then, earnestly to recommend these articles to the immediate and dispassionate attention of the legislatures of the respective states. Let them be candidly reviewed under a sense of the difficulty of combining in one system the various sentiments and interests of a continent divided into so many sovereign and independent communities, under a conviction of the absolute necessity of uniting all our councils and all our strength, to maintain and defend our common liberties….\"\nJournals of the Continental Congress, 1777\nA major weakness of the Articles of Confederation was that they\n\nOptions: \nA. made it too difficult for the government to raise money through taxes and duties\nB. did not include a provision for creating new states\nC. created a too-powerful chief executive\nD. established a single, unified national identity too quickly\nE. denied the federal government the power to mediate disputes between states\nF. granted too much power to the judicial branch\nG. failed to establish a national currency\nH. did not include a mechanism for their own amendment\nI. did not provide for a national army or navy\nJ. allowed for the unrestricted movement of goods and people between states\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
