      "generated_answer": "The excerpt from Roger Williams criticizes state-imposed religion and emphasizes the separation of church and state, reflecting tensions within Puritan society over religious authority and individual conscience. The First Great Awakening was a reaction against the formalism and rigidity of established religious institutions, particularly Puritanism, by emphasizing personal religious experience and emotional revival. Therefore, the movement was a direct response to the decline of religious fervor within Puritanism.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
