      "generated_answer": "The passage reflects William Lloyd Garrison's passionate moral argument for the rights of free Black Americans, grounded in the belief that the Constitution guarantees equal rights regardless of race. This aligns most closely with the goals and principles of the Abolitionist movement, which sought immediate emancipation and full civil rights for African Americans. Garrison’s tone and focus on justice, equality, and constitutional rights are hallmarks of abolitionist rhetoric.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
