      "generated_answer": "The critiques in *Candide* target盲目 optimism, religious hypocrisy, and the injustices of institutions—central themes also found in Rousseau’s skepticism of civilization and progress. Rousseau similarly questioned Enlightenment optimism and the moral corruption of society, aligning closely with Voltaire’s satirical tone. \n\n\\boxed{E}",
