      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}\n\nThe Crimean War (1853–1856) exposed Russia’s military and technological backwardness compared to Western powers, directly motivating Alexander II to enact domestic reforms, including emancipating the serfs, to strengthen the state. While other factors played a role, the immediate impetus was the defeat in Crimea.",
